WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.458
His monitor was

00:00:01.352 --> 00:00:03.026
eating 75% of

00:00:02.838 --> 00:00:03.946
his download speed

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.814
Oscar Molnar pays

00:00:05.626 --> 00:00:07.087
for 2.5 gigabit

00:00:06.899 --> 00:00:07.559
internet

00:00:07.642 --> 00:00:08.668
but saw only

00:00:08.479 --> 00:00:10.165
600 megabits down

00:00:10.354 --> 00:00:11.262
after moving his

00:00:11.074 --> 00:00:12.819
USB Ethernet adapter

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:13.597
onto his Studio

00:00:13.409 --> 00:00:14.635
Display XDR

00:00:15.166 --> 00:00:16.286
Plugged straight into

00:00:16.098 --> 00:00:16.793
his Mac

00:00:16.841 --> 00:00:17.984
the adapter hit

00:00:17.796 --> 00:00:19.305
2.3 gigabits

00:00:19.444 --> 00:00:20.646
Behind the display

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:21.613
it dropped frames

00:00:21.425 --> 00:00:23.441
above about 168

00:00:23.253 --> 00:00:24.467
thousand per second

00:00:24.998 --> 00:00:25.823
The cause

00:00:25.989 --> 00:00:27.097
the adapter sends

00:00:26.908 --> 00:00:28.111
just four USB

00:00:27.923 --> 00:00:29.042
packets per burst

00:00:29.149 --> 00:00:29.974
and the hub's

00:00:29.786 --> 00:00:30.799
go-ahead delay

00:00:30.823 --> 00:00:31.707
makes the drain

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:32.297
slower than the

00:00:32.109 --> 00:00:32.733
input

00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:34.004
Flow control on

00:00:33.816 --> 00:00:34.664
his router got

00:00:34.476 --> 00:00:35.289
him to about

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.186
two gigabits

00:00:36.726 --> 00:00:37.740
Full story on

00:00:37.551 --> 00:00:38.447
the dashboard
